  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Results-Oriented Monitoring (ROM) system for the EU external action</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;The Results Oriented Monitoring (ROM) system is a core component of the European Union&apos;s approach to enhancing the performance and impact of its global interventions under the Directorate-General for International Partnerships (DG INTPA). &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: black;&quot;&gt;ROM serves as an independent assessment tool designed to review ongoing EU-funded interventions against criteria such as relevance, efficiency, effectiveness, and sustainability. Its overarching goal is to improve the design, implementation, and outcomes of these interventions, thus enhancing their overall impact. By providing impartial and evidence-based assessments, ROM facilitates informed decision-making processes within the EU, aiding in accountability and transparency. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;Its main purpose is to enhance the implementation of ongoing interventions, improve the design of future interventions, programmes, and policies through feedback and lessons learned, and provide a basis for accountability.  &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;The Overall Objective of this action is to improve the performance of EU-funded interventions by strengthening design and monitoring systems at intervention and institutional level.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;The Specific Objective of this action is to provide an external, objective, and impartial assessment on the performance of selected ongoing EU-funded interventions, to support the design of on-going interventions or under formulation and to support knowledge management of M&amp;E findings.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(13, 13, 13);&quot;&gt;The Outputs to be delivered by this action contributing to the corresponding Specific Objective are: ROM reviews; new M&amp;amp;E tools; support to design of logframes and monitoring systems at intervention level (SDL); knowledge-based products and studies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
